  "title": "Legal minimum drafts as documents: privacy policy, imprint placeholder, subprocessor list, DPA and beta agreement templates",
  "spec": "Why: marketing/app/privacy/page.tsx:7 and imprint/page.tsx:7 are placeholders; personal data cannot legally be collected from outside users (roadmap 3.3, P0-9). Human decisions 2026-10-06: NO legal entity exists yet; drafts only, unpublished, with \"[entity to be founded]\" placeholders; product name, domain and US-vs-EU hosting are open (use \"[product name]\", \"[domain]\"). The product is a GENERAL tool for any team, globally, English-first: no country or industry niche in the text.\nWhat: write under docs/legal/ (Markdown, plain English, no legal advice claims):\n1. privacy-policy.md: controller \"[entity to be founded], Switzerland\"; what is processed (account email, screen frames of the chosen window, transcripts, screen events, Work Maps, usage counters); purposes; legal bases (Swiss nFADP and EU GDPR Art. 6(1)(b) and (f), consent for Teach practice mode which is opt-in and private to the learner); retention (frames per workspace setting, default 30 days; transcripts and Work Maps until deleted by the workspace); recipients = the subprocessor list; international transfers (US vendors under DPF/SCCs, hosting region \"[US or EU, to be decided]\"); rights; off-the-record and redaction described factually (frames are NOT redacted yet, say so).\n2. imprint.md: placeholder block with the fields Swiss and German law require (name, address, contact, register/VAT once founded), all as \"[...]\".\n3. subprocessors.md: table derived from the code: Supabase (auth, Postgres, storage), Vercel (hosting, functions, cron), Anthropic (vision, decisions, Work Map), ElevenLabs (voice agents) and its agent LLM provider Google (gemini-2.5-flash, src/lib/voice/createAgents.ts), GitHub (desktop releases), Sentry (error tracking, EU, once enabled), optional Presidio (self-hosted, no vendor), Jev/TypeSafe AI (optional, only when JEV_API_KEY is set). Columns: purpose, data categories, region, DPA link placeholder.\n4. dpa-template.md and beta-agreement-template.md: short templates with the clauses a design partner expects (roles, instructions, subprocessors, security measures, deletion at end, no training on customer data, beta disclaimer), placeholders throughout.\n5. docs/legal/README.md: status \"UNPUBLISHED DRAFTS, not reviewed by a lawyer, no entity yet\", what must be true before publishing, and a one-line pointer to the roadmap decision 5.6.\nDo not touch marketing/**, README.md, docs/DEPLOY.md. Cite the code paths for every factual claim about processing.",
  "inputs": [],
  "acceptance": [
    "docs/legal/{README,privacy-policy,imprint,subprocessors,dpa-template,beta-agreement-template}.md exist, English, general (no country or industry niche), every unknown as a bracketed placeholder",
    "subprocessors.md lists every external processor the code calls (Supabase, Vercel, Anthropic, ElevenLabs, Google via ElevenLabs, GitHub, Sentry, optional Presidio and Jev) with purpose, data categories, region",
    "privacy-policy.md states factually that frames are not yet redacted, Teach is opt-in and private to the learner, default frame retention 30 days",
    "marketing/** untouched (a guard: git diff --stat shows no marketing files)",
    ".claude/hooks/tests-green.sh wt/THIS-TASK exits 0"
